      "id": "sol.ahsme-1970-p18.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\[ \\begin{gathered} 3+2\\sqrt2=(\\sqrt2+1)^2,\\\\ 3-2\\sqrt2=(\\sqrt2-1)^2, \\end{gathered} \\] and both \\(\\sqrt2+1\\) and \\(\\sqrt2-1\\) are positive, the difference is \\[ (\\sqrt2+1)-(\\sqrt2-1)=2. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
